<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monte Barbaro</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Monte Barbaro is a hill in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, near Calatafimi, on which stand the ruins of the ancient city of Segesta, chief settlement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elymians">Elymians</a>. Its summit holds the remains of the city's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agora">agora</a>, houses and a Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> facing the sea, while the unfinished Doric temple of the 5th century BCE stands on a neighbouring hill. The site was later occupied by a medieval village.</p></div>
